शार् शार् (also written सार्), cl. 10. P.
शारयति, -यितुम्, to be weak or feeble;
to weaken; [cf. rt. शॄ.]

सरङ्ग स-रङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, having colour;
having a nasal sound; (अस्), m. a quadruped; a bird;
[cf. सारङ्ग.]

सर्पण, अम्, n. the act of creeping or gliding;
going tortuously; the flight of an arrow nearly
parallel with the ground.

सार्वभौतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सर्व-भूत),
belonging or relating to all elements or beings, &c.;
comprising all animated beings.
